The most significant demographic event in Balboan history was the population collapse during the [[Great Adonian War]]. The pre-war population of approximately 18 million (1935) was reduced to approximately 11.7 million by 1947, a loss of roughly one-third, attributable to military casualties, civilian deaths during the siege of Sant Cristòfor, famine, disease, and emigration. The population did not recover to its pre-war level until the 1960s. The post-reunification period has seen sustained population growth, driven by natural increase, return migration, and immigration from Kaftia and Fosia.

=== Urbanisation ===

Approximately 72 per cent of the Balboan population lives in urban areas (2026 estimate). Urbanisation is concentrated in the canal corridor and the Aethiopian coastal plain; the interior highlands remain predominantly rural. The five largest cities are Sant Cristòfor (5,200,000), Sant Bart (2,800,000), Novara (2,200,000), Costabella (1,500,000), and Portnou (1,100,000). The Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area, which extends across much of Estret Province, contains approximately 14.5 million people — roughly 41 per cent of the national population.

