=== Migration ===

Balboa has experienced several major waves of migration that have shaped its demographic composition. The [[Redilution]] and Birthing programmes of the post-independence period (1854–1890) brought approximately 200,000 Illypnian settlers to the isthmus, substantially increasing the white proportion of the population. The [[Zong Balboa]] period (1899–1950) brought significant Fosian immigration — Zong, Sinchewese, and other Zongosphere migrants — who settled in the canal corridor and the agricultural districts of Migjorn. The post-reunification period has seen modest immigration from Kaftia (particularly Burawa and Dakare) and from other Lurandian states, though Balboa has not experienced the scale of immigration seen in some other AC member states.

Emigration has also been significant. The Great Adonian War displaced approximately one-third of the pre-war population, and the post-war period saw substantial emigration of the Zong commercial and administrative elite. More recently, out-migration from the interior provinces — particularly Tramuntana and rural Jala — to Sant Cristòfor and Sant Bart has been a persistent trend, driven by the lack of economic opportunity in the highland districts.

Net migration is approximately +0.2 per cent (2025), with immigration slightly exceeding emigration.

== Ethnic groups ==

[[File:Sant Cristofor skyline.jpg|thumb|250px|Sant Cristòfor, the country's largest city and the centre of the multi-ethnic canal corridor economy]]

The population is divided among five principal ethnic groups, the boundaries among which have been shaped by centuries of colonial rule, racial legislation, and post-reunification reform. The classification system used in Balboan censuses and official statistics reflects the historical racial categories of the colonial and rump-state periods, though the [[Twelve Guarantees]] established the principle that all groups are entitled to equal treatment under the law.

